<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0365">Notation <span data-tag="0365">5.3.2.11</span> <span class="named">(The Mapping Simplex)</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  X(0) \xrightarrow {f(1)} X(1) \xrightarrow { f(1) } X(2) \xrightarrow {f(3)} \cdots \xrightarrow {f(n)} X(n), \]
</div>
<p> which we will identify with a functor $\mathscr {F}: [n] \rightarrow \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}$. We denote the homotopy colimit $ \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}(\mathscr {F} )$ by $ \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}( X(0) \rightarrow \cdots \rightarrow X(n) )$, and refer to it as the <em>mapping simplex</em> of the diagram $\mathscr {F}$. </p>
</article>
